    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e5d537d7-c9ba-5ae7-b5c9-a3fcd377a257",
      ":question/problem": "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x &=-16 \\\\ 5x+12y &=20\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $x,y$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+0y &=-16 \\\\ 5x+12y &=20\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 12\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 0 & -16 \\\\ 5 & 12 & 20\\end{array}\\right]\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
